      "writtenOn": "2022-06-16T22:38:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about `CONFIG_HAS_32BIT_LONG` or `CONFIG_LONG_IS_32BIT`? `USE` makes it sound like we\u0027re somehow forcing the size of `long`. \n\nAlternatively, given Evan\u0027s description that this is purely to prevent cherry-picking `printf` formatting changes that would cause problems in old branches, it may be best to choose a less generic name. i.e., purely targeted to the issue we\u0027re working around. Something like `CONFIG_PRINTF_DISABLE_LONG_WORKAROUND` or `CONFIG_PRINTF_HANDLE_LONG_CORRECTLY`.",
      "range": {
